  "text": "\nCreated a project skill at [`.cursor/skills/feature-flag-rollback-migration/SKILL.md`](.cursor/skills/feature-flag-rollback-migration/SKILL.md) that documents the feature flag workflow from this session.\n\n## Skill Summary\n\n**Name:** `feature-flag-rollback-migration`  \n**Purpose:** Gate new implementations behind a feature flag for rollback safety in Grafana.\n\n**Workflow:**\n1. **Add feature flag** – Add to `registry.go` with Name, Description, Stage, FrontendOnly, Owner, Expression.\n2. **Regenerate** – Run `make gen-feature-toggles`.\n3. **Gate implementation** – Use `config.featureToggles.flagName` to choose between new and legacy paths.\n4. **Update tests** – Mock new behavior, reset flag and shared state in `beforeEach`/`afterEach`, and test both flag states.\n\n**Details captured from this session:**\n- Test isolation: reset shared state (e.g. `locationService.push('/')`) between tests when order matters.\n- Save and restore `config.featureToggles` in `afterEach` to avoid leaking into other suites.\n- Use `jest.requireActual` when mocking so other exports (e.g. `useParams`) stay intact.\n- Checklist for verification.\n\nThe skill links to `react-router-migration` for navigation-specific migrations. It is written so it can be reused for other rollback-safe migrations (APIs, UI, etc.), not only navigation.",
