  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's the full diagram:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"User Actions\"\n        UA1[\"Click <Link> / <a>\"]\n        UA2[\"Call locationService.push()\"]\n        UA3[\"Call locationService.partial()\"]\n        UA4[\"Call locationService.replace()\"]\n        UA5[\"Call useNavigate()\"]\n        UA6[\"<Navigate> component\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Navigation Layer\"\n        direction TB\n        LS[\"locationService (singleton)<br/>HistoryWrapper<br/><i>packages/grafana-runtime</i>\"]\n        H4[\"history v4<br/>createBrowserHistory()\"]\n        RN[\"React Router v6<br/>useNavigate() hook\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Router Tree (RoutesWrapper.tsx + AppWrapper.tsx)\"\n        direction TB\n        R5[\"&lt;Router history={locationService.getHistory()}&gt;<br/><b>React Router v5 root</b><br/><i>react-router-dom@5.3.4</i>\"]\n        LSP[\"&lt;LocationServiceProvider&gt;<br/><i>Context for useLocationService()</i>\"]\n        CR[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt;<br/><b>v5 → v6 bridge</b><br/><i>react-router-dom-v5-compat@6.26</i>\"]\n        AC[\"&lt;AppChrome&gt;<br/><i>Shell, nav, sidebar</i>\"]\n        V6R[\"&lt;Routes&gt; / &lt;Route&gt;<br/><b>React Router v6 rendering</b>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Route Resolution\"\n        direction TB\n        GAR[\"getAppRoutes()<br/><i>routes/routes.tsx</i><br/>Flat RouteDescriptor[]\"]\n        GRW[\"&lt;GrafanaRouteWrapper&gt;<br/><i>Auth, role checks</i>\"]\n        GR[\"&lt;GrafanaRoute&gt;<br/><i>Chrome setup, keybindings,<br/>pageview tracking, error boundary</i>\"]\n        PC[\"Page Component<br/><i>Receives: route, location, queryParams</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Route Sources\"\n        direction LR\n        RS1[\"Core routes<br/><i>dashboards, explore, admin...</i>\"]\n        RS2[\"getAlertingRoutes()\"]\n        RS3[\"getPluginCatalogRoutes()\"]\n        RS4[\"getAppPluginRoutes()\"]\n        RS5[\"getDataConnectionsRoutes()\"]\n        RS6[\"getProvisioningRoutes()\"]\n        RS7[\"getProfileRoutes()\"]\n        RS8[\"extraRoutes[]<br/><i>enterprise extensions</i>\"]\n    end\n\n    %% User action flows\n    UA1 -->|\"href\"| R5\n    UA2 --> LS\n    UA3 --> LS\n    UA4 --> LS\n    UA5 --> RN\n    UA6 --> RN\n\n    %% locationService flow\n    LS -->|\"wraps\"| H4\n    H4 -->|\"history.push/replace\"| R5\n    RN -->|\"navigates within\"| CR\n\n    %% Router tree hierarchy\n    R5 --> LSP\n    LSP --> CR\n    CR --> AC\n    AC --> V6R\n\n    %% Route resolution\n    V6R -->|\"matches path\"| GRW\n    GRW -->|\"passes auth\"| GR\n    GR -->|\"Suspense + ErrorBoundary\"| PC\n\n    %% Route composition\n    RS1 --> GAR\n    RS2 --> GAR\n    RS3 --> GAR\n    RS4 --> GAR\n    RS5 --> GAR\n    RS6 --> GAR\n    RS7 --> GAR\n    RS8 --> GAR\n    GAR -->|\"map to <Route>\"| V6R\n\n    %% Styling\n    classDef legacy fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#000\n    classDef modern fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a,color:#000\n    classDef bridge fill:#fef9c3,stroke:#ca8a04,color:#000\n    classDef neutral fill:#e0e7ff,stroke:#4f46e5,color:#000\n\n    class UA2,UA3,UA4,LS,H4 legacy\n    class UA5,UA6,RN modern\n    class CR bridge\n    class R5,V6R,GAR,GRW,GR neutral\n```\n\n### Reading the diagram\n\n**Color coding:**\n- **Red** — Legacy path (`locationService` → `history` v4). This is how ~200+ files navigate today. The singleton `HistoryWrapper` wraps a v4 `history` instance and exposes `.push()`, `.partial()`, `.replace()`.\n- **Green** — Modern path (`useNavigate`). The v6-native approach, used in ~25 files so far (mostly provisioning, some alerting/admin).\n- **Yellow** — The `<CompatRouter>` bridge. This is the key piece that makes both paths work simultaneously. It subscribes to the v5 `<Router>`'s history and re-publishes it as v6 context, so v6 hooks (`useNavigate`, `useLocation`, `useParams`, `<Navigate>`) all work inside the v5 tree.\n- **Blue** — Framework/neutral components that work regardless of which navigation path is used.\n\n### How the two paths converge\n\nBoth paths ultimately cause the same URL change, but through different mechanisms:\n\n1. **Legacy path:** Component calls `locationService.push('/foo')` → `HistoryWrapper` calls `history.push('/foo')` on the v4 history instance → The v5 `<Router>` (which owns that same history instance) re-renders → `<CompatRouter>` propagates the change into v6 context → `<Routes>` matches the new path → `GrafanaRouteWrapper` renders the page.\n\n2. **Modern path:** Component calls `navigate('/foo')` from `useNavigate()` → The compat layer translates this into a navigation on the underlying v5 history → Same re-render cascade as above.\n\nThe `<CompatRouter>` is the linchpin — it bidirectionally syncs the v5 history with v6's internal routing context, so both imperative (`locationService`) and hook-based (`useNavigate`) navigation end up in the same place.\n\n### What the eventual end state looks like\n\nOnce the migration completes:\n- `locationService` singleton and `history` v4 are removed\n- The v5 `<Router>` and `<CompatRouter>` bridge are replaced with a v6-native `createBrowserRouter` or `<BrowserRouter>`\n- All navigation uses `useNavigate()` or `<Link>`/`<Navigate>` from `react-router-dom` v6 directly\n- The `react-router-dom-v5-compat` package is dropped entirely",
