  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the Grafana codebase and its router architecture.\n\n---\n\n## Codebase Overview\n\nGrafana is a large monorepo with a **Go backend** and a **React/TypeScript frontend**.\n\n### Top-Level Structure\n\n| Directory | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `pkg/` | Go backend — services, APIs, infrastructure |\n| `public/app/` | Frontend React application |\n| `packages/` | Shared npm packages (`@grafana/ui`, `@grafana/data`, `@grafana/runtime`, etc.) |\n| `apps/` | Modular backend services using the Grafana App SDK |\n| `scripts/` | Webpack configs, build scripts, tooling |\n| `conf/` | Default configuration templates |\n| `devenv/` | Docker Compose setup for local dev services (Prometheus, Loki, etc.) |\n| `e2e/`, `e2e-playwright/` | End-to-end tests |\n| `kinds/`, `kindsv2/` | CUE schema definitions for Grafana data types |\n\n### Backend (Go)\n\n- **Entry point:** `pkg/cmd/grafana/main.go`\n- **Server init:** `pkg/server/`\n- **Business logic:** `pkg/services/` (user, dashboards, alerting, auth, etc.)\n- **REST API:** `pkg/api/`\n- **Feature flags:** `pkg/services/featuremgmt/`\n- Uses **Wire** for dependency injection (`make gen-go` to regenerate)\n\n### Frontend (React/TypeScript)\n\n- **Entry point:** `public/app/app.ts` — bootstraps i18n, services, Redux store, then renders `AppWrapper`\n- **Core:** `public/app/core/` — shared services, components, navigation\n- **Features:** `public/app/features/` — modular feature areas (dashboard, explore, alerting, etc.)\n- **Plugins:** `public/app/plugins/` — built-in panel and data source plugins\n- Code-split via `SafeDynamicImport` (wrapper around `React.lazy`)\n\n---\n\n## Router Architecture (Detail)\n\n### Tech Stack\n\nGrafana currently uses **React Router v5** with a **v6 compatibility layer**:\n\n- `react-router@5.3.4` / `react-router-dom@5.3.4` (core)\n- `react-router-dom-v5-compat@^6.26.1` (bridge to v6 APIs)\n\nThis lets the codebase incrementally adopt v6 patterns (`Routes`, `Route`, `useNavigate`, `useParams`) while the underlying router is still v5.\n\n### Component Hierarchy\n\n```\nAppWrapper (public/app/AppWrapper.tsx)\n  └── RouterWrapper (public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx)\n        ├── Router (v5, uses locationService.getHistory())\n        ├── LocationServiceProvider\n        ├── CompatRouter (v5→v6 bridge)\n        └── AppChrome (shell: top nav, mega menu, sidebars)\n              └── <Routes> (v6 API via compat)\n                    └── <Route element={<GrafanaRouteWrapper />}>\n                          └── GrafanaRoute\n                                └── route.component (lazy-loaded page)\n```\n\n### Key Files\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Central route registry — `getAppRoutes()` |\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Sets up Router, providers, AppChrome |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Iterates routes, renders `<Routes>` with `<Route>` elements |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Per-route wrapper handling auth, RBAC, and error boundaries |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | `RouteDescriptor` type definition |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | `locationService` singleton |\n\n### Route Registry\n\nAll routes are defined in `getAppRoutes()` inside `public/app/routes/routes.tsx`. Each route is a `RouteDescriptor`:\n\n```typescript\ninterface RouteDescriptor {\n  path: string;\n  component: GrafanaRouteComponent;  // lazy-loaded\n  roles?: () => string[];            // RBAC roles\n  chromeless?: boolean;              // hide AppChrome shell\n  sensitive?: boolean;               // case-sensitive matching\n  allowAnonymous?: boolean | ((params) => boolean);\n}\n```\n\nRoutes are aggregated from multiple sources:\n- **Core routes** defined inline (dashboards, explore, admin, login, etc.)\n- **Feature routes** from dedicated modules: `getAlertingRoutes()`, `getProfileRoutes()`, `getDataConnectionsRoutes()`, `getProvisioningRoutes()`, etc.\n- **Plugin routes** via `getAppPluginRoutes()` — plugins can register standalone pages or even override core pages\n- **Catch-all 404** at the end\n\n### Route Rendering\n\nIn `AppWrapper.tsx`, routes are rendered like this:\n\n```typescript\nrenderRoute = (route: RouteDescriptor) => (\n  <Route\n    caseSensitive={route.sensitive ?? false}\n    path={route.path}\n    key={route.path}\n    element={<GrafanaRouteWrapper route={route} />}\n  />\n);\n\nrenderRoutes() {\n  return <Routes>{getAppRoutes().map((r) => this.renderRoute(r))}</Routes>;\n}\n```\n\n### GrafanaRouteWrapper — Auth & RBAC Guard\n\n`GrafanaRouteWrapper` in `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` runs before every route:\n\n1. **Login check** — if the route requires auth and the user isn't signed in, redirects to `/login`\n2. **Role check** — if the route specifies `roles`, verifies the user has one of them; otherwise redirects to `/`\n3. Passes through to `GrafanaRoute` which renders the actual page component\n\n### locationService\n\n`locationService` is the historical navigation abstraction, a singleton wrapping the `history` library:\n\n```typescript\ninterface LocationService {\n  push(location): void;       // navigate to a new URL\n  replace(location): void;    // replace current URL\n  partial(query, replace?): void; // merge query params\n  getHistory(): History;       // used by the v5 Router\n  getLocation(): Location;\n  getSearch(): URLSearchParams;\n  getSearchObject(): UrlQueryMap;\n}\n```\n\nIt's used extensively across the codebase (~80+ files use `push`, ~50+ use `partial`). A link click interceptor (`public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts`) catches all `<a>` tag clicks and routes them through `locationService.push()` instead of triggering full page reloads.\n\n### AppChrome (Shell)\n\n`AppChrome` in `public/app/core/components/AppChrome/` wraps all routes and provides:\n- Top navigation bar\n- Mega menu (sidebar)\n- Command palette\n- Extension sidebar\n- Routes marked `chromeless: true` (like embedded panels via `/d-solo/:uid`) skip the shell entirely\n\n### React Router Migration (v5 → v6 / useNavigate)\n\nThere's an active, incremental migration underway:\n\n| Status | Areas |\n|---|---|\n| **Migrated** | Provisioning features (no feature flag needed) |\n| **In progress (feature-flagged)** | Playlists, Teams, Service Accounts |\n| **Not yet started** | Dashboard, Explore, Alerting, Data sources, Browse dashboards, and many others |\n| **Last to migrate** | Shared infra (`useUrlParams`, `useQueryParams`, `interceptLinkClicks`) |\n\nThe migration pattern replaces `locationService.push/replace/partial` calls with React Router v6's `useNavigate()` hook:\n\n```typescript\n// Before (locationService)\nlocationService.push('/some/path');\n\n// After (React Router v6)\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\nnavigate('/some/path');\n```\n\nFeature flags (e.g., `playlistUseNavigate`, `teamsUseNavigate`) gate the rollout per area. The v5-compat bridge allows both patterns to coexist during the transition.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nGrafana's frontend is a large single-page application with a centralized route registry, lazy-loaded page components, and a custom navigation abstraction (`locationService`) layered over React Router v5. The app is mid-migration to React Router v6 APIs via a compatibility bridge, with the goal of eventually replacing `locationService` usage with native `useNavigate` hooks throughout.",
