  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's the full picture.\n\n## Navigation Flow Diagram\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"User Action\"\n        A[\"User clicks link / submits form / triggers event\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Two Navigation Paths\"\n        B[\"Legacy: locationService.push('/path')\"]\n        C[\"Modern: const navigate = useNavigate();\\n navigate('/path')\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"LocationService (HistoryWrapper)\"\n        D[\"HistoryWrapper.push()\"]\n        E[\"HistoryWrapper.replace()\"]\n        F[\"HistoryWrapper.partial()\"]\n        G[\"this.history (H.History instance)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"React Router v5 Layer\"\n        H[\"&lt;Router history={locationService.getHistory()}&gt;\"]\n        I[\"v5 Router listens to history changes\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"v5 ↔ v6 Compatibility Bridge\"\n        J[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt;\\nBridges v5 history to v6 APIs\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"React Router v6 APIs (via compat)\"\n        K[\"&lt;Routes&gt; / &lt;Route&gt;\"]\n        L[\"useNavigate()\"]\n        M[\"useLocation()\"]\n        N[\"useParams()\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Route Resolution\"\n        O[\"RouteDescriptor[] from getAppRoutes()\"]\n        P[\"GrafanaRouteWrapper\\n- Auth check\\n- RBAC role check\"]\n        Q[\"GrafanaRoute\\n- ErrorBoundary\\n- Suspense\\n- Renders component\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Layout Shell\"\n        R[\"AppChrome\\n(top nav, mega menu, sidebar)\"]\n        S[\"Route Component Rendered\"]\n    end\n\n    A --> B\n    A --> C\n\n    B --> D\n    B --> E\n    B --> F\n    D --> G\n    E --> G\n    F --> G\n\n    C -->|\"calls history under the hood\"| J\n\n    G -->|\"same History instance\"| H\n    H --> I\n    I --> J\n    J --> K\n\n    K --> O\n    O --> P\n    P -->|\"auth passes\"| Q\n    P -->|\"auth fails\"| T[\"&lt;Navigate to='/login' /&gt;\"]\n    P -->|\"role fails\"| U[\"&lt;Navigate to='/' /&gt;\"]\n\n    Q --> R\n    R --> S\n\n    L -.->|\"provided by CompatRouter\"| J\n    M -.->|\"provided by CompatRouter\"| J\n    N -.->|\"provided by CompatRouter\"| J\n\n    style B fill:#f9e0e0,stroke:#c44\n    style C fill:#e0f0e0,stroke:#4a4\n    style J fill:#e0e8f8,stroke:#44c\n    style G fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#b80\n```\n\n### How to read this\n\n**The critical insight** is that both paths converge on the same `History` instance:\n\n1. **Legacy path (red)** — Component imports `locationService` from `@grafana/runtime` and calls `locationService.push()`. This delegates to `this.history.push()` inside `HistoryWrapper`.\n\n2. **Modern path (green)** — Component calls `useNavigate()` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`. Under the hood, `CompatRouter` (blue) provides this hook, which also manipulates the same history instance.\n\n3. **Shared history** (yellow) — The v5 `<Router>` is initialized with `locationService.getHistory()`, so the `History` object is the single source of truth. Both `locationService` and `useNavigate` write to it, and the Router listens for changes on it.\n\n4. **Route resolution** — When the URL changes, `<Routes>` matches against the `RouteDescriptor[]` from `getAppRoutes()`. The matched route passes through `GrafanaRouteWrapper` (auth + RBAC checks), then `GrafanaRoute` (error boundary + suspense), and finally renders inside `AppChrome`.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Starter Files\n\nThese are functional components with a **single** `locationService.push()` call and fewer than ~120 lines — ideal for a first migration pass:\n\n| File | Lines | locationService Call | What It Does |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistNewPage.tsx` | 40 | `locationService.push('/playlists')` | Navigates after creating a playlist |\n| `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistEditPage.tsx` | 53 | `locationService.push('/playlists')` | Navigates after editing a playlist |\n| `public/app/features/dashboard-scene/v2schema/ImportDashboardOverviewV2.tsx` | 84 | `locationService.push(dashboardUrl)` | Navigates after importing a dashboard |\n| `public/app/features/teams/CreateTeam.tsx` | 121 | `locationService.push('/org/teams/edit/${uid}')` | Navigates after creating a team |\n| `public/app/features/playlist/StartModal.tsx` | 121 | `locationService.push(url)` | Navigates to start a playlist |\n\n### Migration pattern for each\n\nThe change in each file is mechanical:\n\n```typescript\n// Before (legacy)\nimport { locationService } from '@grafana/runtime';\n\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const onSave = () => {\n    locationService.push('/some/path');\n  };\n}\n\n// After (modern)\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate();\n  const onSave = () => {\n    navigate('/some/path');\n  };\n}\n```\n\nFor `locationService.replace()`, the equivalent is `navigate('/path', { replace: true })`.\n\nThe playlist files (`PlaylistNewPage`, `PlaylistEditPage`) are the lowest-risk starting points — they're tiny, self-contained, and have a single straightforward navigation call.",
