  "text": "\nCreated the skill at `.cursor/skills/grafana-feature-flag-gating/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Skill: `grafana-feature-flag-gating`\n\n**Purpose:** Describes Grafana’s feature flag gating workflow for safe rollout and rollback.\n\n**When it applies:** When adding feature-flagged behavior, migrating components with rollback safety, or when feature flags, gating, or rollback are mentioned.\n\n**Workflow:**\n\n1. **Registry** — Add the flag to `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go` with the usual fields (Name, Description, Stage, FrontendOnly, Owner, Expression).\n2. **Regenerate** — Run `make gen-feature-toggles` to update generated artifacts.\n3. **Component** — Use `if (config.featureToggles.flagName) { newBehavior } else { oldBehavior }` and keep both paths.\n4. **Tests** — Reset the flag in `beforeEach`/`afterEach`, mock new dependencies, and add tests for both flag-on and flag-off.\n\nThe skill also links to `react-router-migration` for navigation-specific migrations. Future agents can use it for any feature-flagged rollout in Grafana.",
