{
  "conversation_id": "c4588fa2-6e75-4504-92b1-96ee027e3521",
  "generation_id": "3e170566-f4db-4ed8-88c9-0a84e7c2ce91",
  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "## Grafana Codebase Overview\n\nGrafana is a large-scale observability platform built as a **monorepo** with a Go backend and React/TypeScript frontend, managed with Yarn Workspaces and Nx for build orchestration.\n\n### Top-Level Structure\n\n| Directory | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| `pkg/` | Backend Go code — services, APIs, middleware, storage |\n| `public/app/` | Frontend React/TypeScript application |\n| `packages/` | Shared npm packages (`@grafana/ui`, `@grafana/data`, `@grafana/runtime`, etc.) |\n| `apps/` | Modular Grafana App SDK services (dashboard, alerting, IAM, etc.) |\n| `conf/` | Configuration files and templates |\n| `scripts/` | Build scripts, code generation, CI utilities |\n| `devenv/` | Docker Compose dev environment |\n| `e2e-playwright/` | Playwright E2E tests |\n| `kinds/` / `kindsv2/` | CUE schema definitions |\n\n### Technology Stack\n\n- **Backend:** Go 1.25, Wire (DI), custom HTTP server, PostgreSQL/MySQL/SQLite, Kubernetes API machinery\n- **Frontend:** React 18, TypeScript 5.9, Webpack 5 (via Nx), Redux Toolkit\n- **Routing:** React Router v5.3.4 with a v6 compatibility bridge\n- **Package Manager:** Yarn 4 (workspaces), Nx 21\n\n### Key Entry Points\n\n- **Backend:** `pkg/cmd/grafana/main.go` (CLI), `pkg/server/` (server init + Wire)\n- **Frontend:** `public/app/app.ts` (React app bootstrap), `public/app/routes/` (routing)\n\n---\n\n## React Router Architecture (In Depth)\n\n### Version & Compatibility Strategy\n\nGrafana runs **React Router v5** at the top level but uses `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (v6 bridge) throughout. This allows the codebase to incrementally adopt v6 APIs (`useNavigate`, `useLocation`, `useParams`, `<Routes>`, `<Route>`) while the root `<Router>` still uses v5's history-based API.\n\n### The Router Hierarchy\n\nThe nesting looks like this:\n\n```\n<Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>     ← v5 Router (history object)\n  <LocationServiceProvider>\n    <CompatRouter>                                   ← v6 compatibility bridge\n      <QueriesDrawerContextProvider>\n        <AppChrome>                                  ← Shell (nav, sidebar, etc.)\n          <Routes>                                   ← v6 route matching\n            <Route element={<GrafanaRouteWrapper>}>  ← Auth/RBAC guard\n              <route.component />                    ← Lazy-loaded page\n            </Route>\n          </Routes>\n        </AppChrome>\n      </QueriesDrawerContextProvider>\n    </CompatRouter>\n  </LocationServiceProvider>\n</Router>\n```\n\n### Key Routing Files\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Sets up the Router + CompatRouter + context providers |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Central route registry — `getAppRoutes()` returns `RouteDescriptor[]` |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | Maps `RouteDescriptor` array into `<Routes>` / `<Route>` elements |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Per-route wrapper handling auth, RBAC, and error boundaries |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/types.ts` | `RouteDescriptor` type definition |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` | Global `<a>` click interception for SPA navigation |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | `locationService` singleton (legacy navigation API) |\n\n### Route Definition Pattern\n\nRoutes are defined centrally in `routes.tsx` as `RouteDescriptor` objects, aggregating sub-routes from features:\n\n```typescript\n// public/app/routes/routes.tsx\nexport function getAppRoutes(): RouteDescriptor[] {\n  return [\n    { path: '/', component: SafeDynamicImport(...) },\n    ...getAlertingRoutes(),\n    ...getProfileRoutes(),\n    ...getProvisioningRoutes(),\n    // ~500+ lines of route definitions\n  ];\n}\n```\n\nEach route uses `SafeDynamicImport` (a wrapper around `React.lazy`) for code-splitting.\n\n### Route Guards\n\nAuthentication and RBAC are handled in `GrafanaRoute.tsx`:\n\n- **Auth check:** If the route doesn't allow anonymous access and the user isn't signed in, it redirects to `/login` via `<Navigate replace to=\"/login\" />`\n- **RBAC check:** If the route specifies `roles`, it checks `contextSrv.hasRole()` and redirects to `/` if the user lacks the required role\n- **Error boundary:** Catches rendering errors and shows `GrafanaRouteError`\n\n### Navigation: Two Competing Patterns\n\n**1. Legacy — `locationService` (dominant, ~150+ files)**\n\n```typescript\nimport { locationService } from '@grafana/runtime';\n\nlocationService.push('/dashboards');\nlocationService.replace('/login');\nlocationService.partial({ tab: 'settings' }); // update query params\n```\n\nThis is a singleton wrapping a `history` object, available anywhere (inside or outside React components).\n\n**2. Modern — `useNavigate` (growing, ~85 files)**\n\n```typescript\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\nnavigate('/dashboards');\nnavigate('/dashboards', { replace: true });\n```\n\nThis is the standard React Router v6 hook, only usable inside React components.\n\n### Migration Status (~40% complete)\n\nThe codebase is actively migrating from `locationService` to `useNavigate`. The migration uses **feature flags** to gate the transition per feature area:\n\n| Area | Status | Feature Flag |\n|------|--------|-------------|\n| Provisioning | Migrated | None needed |\n| Playlists | In progress | `playlistUseNavigate` |\n| Teams | In progress | `teamsUseNavigate` |\n| Service Accounts | In progress | Feature-flagged |\n| Dashboards | Not started | — |\n| Alerting | Not started | — |\n| Explore | Not started | — |\n\nThe migration pattern typically looks like:\n\n```typescript\nif (config.featureToggles.featureUseNavigate) {\n  const navigate = useNavigate();\n  navigate('/path');\n} else {\n  locationService.push('/path');\n}\n```\n\nShared infrastructure hooks like `useUrlParams()` and `useQueryParams()` still use `locationService` internally and will be migrated last.\n\n### Link Click Interception\n\n`interceptLinkClicks.ts` globally intercepts `<a>` tag clicks to enable SPA navigation. It checks whether the link is internal, not modified by keyboard shortcuts, and not targeting a new window — then routes through `locationService.push()` instead of a full page load.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nGrafana's routing is in a transitional state: a v5 `<Router>` at the root with a v6 `<CompatRouter>` bridge enables incremental adoption of v6 hooks. Routes are centrally defined in `routes.tsx`, lazy-loaded, and guarded by `GrafanaRoute`. Navigation is migrating feature-by-feature from the `locationService` singleton to `useNavigate`, gated by feature flags, with roughly 40% of the codebase converted so far.",
