  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here are the diagrams and migration recommendations.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Relationship Between locationService, React Router, and useNavigate\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"Browser\"\n        URL[\"Browser URL Bar\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"History Layer\"\n        H[\"history (v4 package)<br/>createBrowserHistory()\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"locationService Singleton\"\n        LS[\"HistoryWrapper\"]\n        LSPush[\"push(path)\"]\n        LSReplace[\"replace(path)\"]\n        LSPartial[\"partial(query)\"]\n        LSGetHistory[\"getHistory()\"]\n        LSObservable[\"BehaviorSubject&lt;Location&gt;\"]\n        LS --- LSPush & LSReplace & LSPartial & LSGetHistory & LSObservable\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"React Router v5\"\n        RV5[\"&lt;Router history={...}&gt;\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Compatibility Bridge\"\n        CR[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt;<br/>react-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"React Router v6 APIs\"\n        Routes[\"&lt;Routes&gt; / &lt;Route&gt;\"]\n        UN[\"useNavigate()\"]\n        UL[\"useLocation()\"]\n        UP[\"useParams()\"]\n        Nav[\"&lt;Navigate&gt;\"]\n    end\n\n    LSGetHistory -->|\"provides history object\"| RV5\n    RV5 -->|\"wraps children\"| CR\n    CR -->|\"enables v6 hooks\"| Routes & UN & UL & UP & Nav\n\n    LSPush & LSReplace & LSPartial -->|\"mutate\"| H\n    UN -->|\"mutate\"| H\n    H <-->|\"syncs\"| URL\n    H -->|\"listen()\"| LSObservable\n    H -->|\"triggers re-render\"| RV5\n\n    style LS fill:#f9e2af,stroke:#e6a817\n    style CR fill:#89b4fa,stroke:#1d6ce0\n    style UN fill:#a6e3a1,stroke:#40a02b\n    style H fill:#f38ba8,stroke:#d20f39\n```\n\n**Key insight:** Both `locationService` and `useNavigate` ultimately mutate the same `history` object. The `locationService` wraps it as a singleton accessible anywhere; `useNavigate` accesses it through React context. They are two doors to the same room.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Navigation Flow: User Action to URL Change\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Component as React Component\n    participant LS as locationService\n    participant Nav as useNavigate()\n    participant History as history object\n    participant Router as v5 Router\n    participant Compat as CompatRouter\n    participant Routes as Routes/Route (v6)\n    participant Guard as GrafanaRouteWrapper\n    participant Page as Page Component\n\n    alt Legacy Path (locationService)\n        User->>Component: clicks button / submits form\n        Component->>LS: locationService.push(\"/new-path\")\n        LS->>History: history.push(\"/new-path\")\n    end\n\n    alt Modern Path (useNavigate)\n        User->>Component: clicks button / submits form\n        Component->>Nav: navigate(\"/new-path\")\n        Nav->>History: history.push(\"/new-path\")\n    end\n\n    alt Link Click Interception\n        User->>Component: clicks <a href=\"/path\">\n        Component->>Component: interceptLinkClicks(event)\n        Component->>Component: e.preventDefault()\n        Component->>LS: locationService.push(\"/path\")\n        LS->>History: history.push(\"/path\")\n    end\n\n    History->>Router: triggers re-render (location changed)\n    Router->>Compat: propagates new location\n    Compat->>Routes: v6 route matching\n    Routes->>Guard: GrafanaRouteWrapper receives route\n    Guard->>Guard: check auth (isSignedIn?)\n    Guard->>Guard: check RBAC roles\n\n    alt Unauthorized\n        Guard->>History: <Navigate to=\"/login\" />\n    end\n\n    alt Authorized\n        Guard->>Page: render route.component (lazy loaded)\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. v5-to-v6 Compatibility Layer Breakdown\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"v5 Layer (Current Root)\"\n        direction TB\n        R5Router[\"&lt;Router history={locationService.getHistory()}&gt;<br/><i>from react-router-dom (v5)</i>\"]\n        R5Context[\"v5 Router Context<br/>• match<br/>• location<br/>• history\"]\n        R5Router --> R5Context\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Bridge Layer\"\n        direction TB\n        LSProvider[\"&lt;LocationServiceProvider&gt;<br/><i>provides locationService via React context</i>\"]\n        CompatRouter[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt;<br/><i>from react-router-dom-v5-compat</i><br/><br/>Reads v5 context ↓<br/>Creates v6 context ↓\"]\n        R6Context[\"v6 Router Context<br/>• navigation<br/>• location<br/>• outlet\"]\n        LSProvider --> CompatRouter --> R6Context\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"v6 API Layer (Consumer Code)\"\n        direction TB\n        Routes[\"&lt;Routes&gt; + &lt;Route&gt;<br/><i>v6 declarative routing</i>\"]\n        Hooks[\"Hooks:<br/>• useNavigate()<br/>• useLocation()<br/>• useParams()<br/>• useSearchParams()\"]\n        Components[\"Components:<br/>• &lt;Navigate&gt;<br/>• &lt;Outlet&gt;<br/>• &lt;Link&gt;\"]\n    end\n\n    R5Context -->|\"CompatRouter reads<br/>v5 location + history\"| CompatRouter\n    R6Context --> Routes & Hooks & Components\n\n    subgraph \"Import Sources\"\n        direction LR\n        V5Import[\"react-router-dom<br/>(v5.3.4)\"]\n        CompatImport[\"react-router-dom-v5-compat<br/>(~v6.26)\"]\n    end\n\n    V5Import -.->|\"Router only\"| R5Router\n    CompatImport -.->|\"everything else\"| Routes & Hooks & Components\n\n    style CompatRouter fill:#89b4fa,stroke:#1d6ce0\n    style R5Router fill:#f9e2af,stroke:#e6a817\n    style Routes fill:#a6e3a1,stroke:#40a02b\n    style Hooks fill:#a6e3a1,stroke:#40a02b\n    style Components fill:#a6e3a1,stroke:#40a02b\n```\n\n**What the compat layer does:** `<CompatRouter>` subscribes to the v5 router context (which gets `location` and `history` from the v5 `<Router>`), then re-provides them as a v6 router context. This allows all child components to use v6 hooks like `useNavigate()` and v6 components like `<Routes>`, even though the root router is still v5.\n\n**What's imported from where:**\n- `react-router-dom` (v5): Only `Router` in `RoutesWrapper.tsx`\n- `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (v6): Everything else — `Routes`, `Route`, `useNavigate`, `useLocation`, `useParams`, `Navigate`\n\n---\n\n## 4. Recommended Files for a Small-Scale Migration\n\nBased on the existing migration pattern documented in the repo's skill file, here are the best candidates ranked by simplicity:\n\n### Tier 1: Trivially Simple (start here)\n\n| File | Lines | Usage | Why It's Easy |\n|------|-------|-------|---------------|\n| `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistNewPage.tsx` | 39 | Single `locationService.push('/playlists')` | Smallest file, one nav call after form submit |\n| `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistEditPage.tsx` | 52 | Single `locationService.push('/playlists')` | Nearly identical pattern to PlaylistNewPage |\n\n### Tier 2: Small and Self-Contained\n\n| File | Lines | Usage | Why It's Easy |\n|------|-------|-------|---------------|\n| `public/app/features/playlist/StartModal.tsx` | 120 | Single `locationService.push(url)` | Self-contained modal, one nav call |\n| `public/app/features/teams/CreateTeam.tsx` | 120 | Single `locationService.push(...)` | Simple form, navigates on success |\n| `public/app/features/org/UserInviteForm.tsx` | 133 | Single `locationService.push('/admin/users/')` | Simple form, one nav call |\n\n### Tier 3: Slightly More Complex\n\n| File | Lines | Usage | Why It's Easy |\n|------|-------|-------|---------------|\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/components/CreateNewButton.tsx` | 184 | Single `locationService.push(...)` | One nav call, but more surrounding logic |\n| `public/app/features/serviceaccounts/ServiceAccountCreatePage.tsx` | 208 | Single `locationService.push(...)` | One nav call on creation success |\n\n### Recommended Starting Path\n\nI'd recommend starting with the **Playlist feature** (`PlaylistNewPage.tsx` + `PlaylistEditPage.tsx`) because:\n\n1. They're the smallest files (39 and 52 lines)\n2. Each has exactly one `locationService.push()` call\n3. They're functional components with hooks already in use\n4. The playlist feature already has a `playlistUseNavigate` flag pattern established in the codebase, so you can follow existing precedent exactly\n5. They navigate to the same path (`/playlists`), so testing is straightforward\n\n### Migration Steps (per the repo's skill)\n\nFor each file, the pattern is:\n\n1. **Add feature flag** in `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go` (e.g., `playlistUseNavigate`)\n2. **Run** `make gen-feature-toggles`\n3. **Add imports** — `useNavigate` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` and `config` from `@grafana/runtime`\n4. **Add hook** — `const navigate = useNavigate();` at the top of the component\n5. **Gate the call:**\n\n```typescript\n// Before\nlocationService.push('/playlists');\n\n// After\nif (config.featureToggles.playlistUseNavigate) {\n  navigate('/playlists');\n} else {\n  locationService.push('/playlists');\n}\n```\n\n6. **Add tests** covering both the flag-on and flag-off paths\n\nThe key constraint: always import `useNavigate` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat` (not `react-router-dom`), since the v6 context is provided by `<CompatRouter>`, not a native v6 `<BrowserRouter>`.",
