  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the files that make up the Bookmarks page UI.\n\n## Core Page Component\n\n- **`public/app/features/bookmarks/BookmarksPage.tsx`** (67 lines) — The main page component. Reads pinned items via `usePinnedItems()`, resolves nav items, and renders a grid of `NavLandingPageCard` components or an empty state.\n\n## Shared UI Components\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/NavLandingPage/NavLandingPageCard.tsx`** (89 lines) — The reusable card component used by `BookmarksPage` to render each individual bookmark entry.\n\n## MegaMenu Integration (Pin/Unpin)\n\nThese are the files that handle how bookmarks appear in the side navigation and how users pin/unpin items:\n\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenu.tsx`** (174 lines) — Main mega menu; populates the bookmarks section with pinned items.\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenuItem.tsx`** (241 lines) — Individual menu item with pin/unpin functionality.\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/MegaMenuItemText.tsx`** (132 lines) — Renders the pin icon button (visible on hover) that toggles bookmarks.\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/hooks.ts`** (13 lines) — Exports `usePinnedItems` hook; fetches `bookmarkUrls` from user preferences via RTK Query.\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/utils.ts`** (199 lines) — Utility functions including `findByUrl`, which resolves bookmark URLs to nav model items. Used by both `BookmarksPage` and `MegaMenu`.\n\n## State Management\n\n- **`public/app/core/reducers/navBarTree.ts`** (99 lines) — Redux reducer that exports the `setBookmark` action for adding/removing bookmark children from the nav tree.\n\n## Routing\n\n- **`public/app/routes/routes.tsx`** (~line 537) — Registers the `/bookmarks` path with a lazy-loaded `BookmarksPage`.\n\n## Backend (Nav Tree & Preferences API)\n\n- **`pkg/services/navtree/navtreeimpl/navtree.go`** (~line 188) — Creates the \"Bookmarks\" nav section in the backend nav tree.\n- **`pkg/services/navtree/models.go`** — Defines `NavIDBookmarks = \"bookmarks\"` and `WeightBookmarks` constants.\n- **`pkg/services/preference/prefapi/api.go`** (~line 115) — Handles the `BookmarkUrls` field when getting/saving user preferences.\n\n## Types & API Clients\n\n- **`packages/grafana-schema/src/raw/preferences/x/preferences_types.gen.ts`** — Generated types with `NavbarPreference.bookmarkUrls: Array<string>`.\n- **`packages/grafana-api-clients/src/clients/rtkq/preferences/user/endpoints.gen.ts`** — Generated RTK Query endpoints and types for preferences including bookmarks.\n\n## Translations\n\n- **`public/app/core/utils/navBarItem-translations.ts`** (~line 26) — Translations for `'bookmarks'` and `'bookmarks-empty'` message IDs.\n- Additional translation keys: `bookmarks-page.empty.message`, `bookmarks-page.empty.tip`, `navigation.item.add-bookmark`, `navigation.item.remove-bookmark`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **`e2e-playwright/various-suite/bookmarks.spec.ts`** (95 lines) — Playwright E2E tests covering pin/unpin, bookmark visibility in the menu, and persistence.\n- **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/utils.test.ts`** (194 lines) — Unit tests for `findByUrl` and `getActiveItem` with bookmark-related mock data.\n\n## Data Flow Summary\n\n1. User preferences store a `bookmarkUrls` string array\n2. Backend serves via `/api/user/preferences` (GET/PATCH)\n3. Frontend reads via `usePinnedItems()` → RTK Query → `useGetUserPreferencesQuery`\n4. `BookmarksPage` resolves URLs to nav items using `findByUrl` and renders them as cards\n5. Pin/unpin actions update preferences via `usePatchUserPreferencesMutation` and dispatch `setBookmark` to Redux\n\nFor UI updates, you'll most likely want to focus on `BookmarksPage.tsx` and `NavLandingPageCard.tsx` as the primary rendering components, with `hooks.ts` and `utils.ts` providing the data layer.",
