  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the React Router migration in Grafana.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n### Current State: Dual-Router Compatibility Layer\n\nGrafana is migrating from **React Router v5** (with a custom `locationService` abstraction) to **React Router v6**. The migration uses a **compatibility shim** (`react-router-dom-v5-compat`) so that v5 and v6 APIs can coexist during the transition.\n\nThe router setup lives in `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx`:\n\n```27:54:public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx\nexport function RouterWrapper(props: RouterWrapperProps) {\n  return (\n    <Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>\n      <LocationServiceProvider service={locationService}>\n        <CompatRouter>\n          // ... app shell\n        </CompatRouter>\n      </LocationServiceProvider>\n    </Router>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThree layers are nested:\n\n1. **`<Router history={...}>`** — the v5 router, using the history object from `locationService`\n2. **`<LocationServiceProvider>`** — makes the legacy `locationService` singleton available via React context\n3. **`<CompatRouter>`** — the v5-compat bridge that lets v6 hooks (`useNavigate`, `useParams`, etc.) work inside the v5 router tree\n\n### The Legacy: `locationService`\n\nDefined in `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx`, this is a **singleton** wrapping a `history` object from the `history` npm package. It exposes three navigation methods:\n\n- **`push(path)`** — navigate to a new URL (adds to history stack)\n- **`replace(path)`** — navigate without adding to history stack\n- **`partial(query, replace?)`** — merge query parameters into the current URL\n\nThis is a non-React, imperative API. Components import it directly and call it anywhere — in event handlers, thunks, utilities, etc. The problem: it bypasses React's rendering lifecycle and doesn't compose with React Router's data APIs.\n\n### The Target: `useNavigate`\n\nThe React Router v6 `useNavigate` hook returns a `navigate` function that is React-context-aware. The migration replaces `locationService.push/replace` calls with `navigate(path)` / `navigate(path, { replace: true })`.\n\n### Migration Strategy: Feature-Flagged, Per-Area\n\nEach area of the UI gets its own feature flag (e.g., `playlistUseNavigate`, `dashboardUseNavigate`). During migration, navigation calls are branched:\n\n```typescript\nif (config.featureToggles.playlistUseNavigate) {\n  navigate('/playlists');\n} else {\n  locationService.push('/playlists');\n}\n```\n\nThis allows incremental rollout and safe rollback per feature area.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Progress\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|--------|-------|\n| Files still using `locationService` navigation (non-test) | ~118 |\n| Files already using `useNavigate` compat | ~17 |\n| Partially migrated files | 1 |\n| Estimated completion | ~40% hooks/components, ~60% remaining |\n\nThe bulk of remaining work is in `public/app/features/` — dashboards, explore, alerting, plugins admin, and various settings pages.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Starter Files\n\nThese are small, self-contained files with only **1 `locationService` call** each — ideal for learning the migration pattern:\n\n| File | Calls | Why it's a good starter |\n|------|-------|------------------------|\n| `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistNewPage.tsx` | 1 | Single redirect after form submit; clean component |\n| `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistEditPage.tsx` | 1 | Same pattern as `PlaylistNewPage`; easy to do both together |\n| `public/app/features/teams/CreateTeam.tsx` | 1 | One post-create redirect; simple async flow |\n| `public/app/features/org/UserInviteForm.tsx` | 1 | Single redirect after dispatch; form logic unaffected |\n| `public/app/features/playlist/StartModal.tsx` | 1 | Self-contained modal with one navigate action |\n| `public/app/features/plugins/admin/hooks/useHistory.tsx` | 1 | Tiny adapter hook; the most localized change possible |\n\nThe **playlist files** (`PlaylistNewPage`, `PlaylistEditPage`, `StartModal`) are particularly nice because they form a small, cohesive feature area — you could migrate all three under a single `playlistUseNavigate` feature flag.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Workflow (Summary)\n\n1. **Add a feature flag** in `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go` (naming convention: `{area}UseNavigate`)\n2. **Run `make gen-feature-toggles`** to generate TypeScript types\n3. **In the component**: import `useNavigate` from `react-router-dom-v5-compat`, call it at the top level\n4. **Replace navigation calls** with a feature-flag branch (`config.featureToggles.yourFlag ? navigate(...) : locationService.push(...)`)\n5. **Update tests** to cover both branches using `jest.mock` for `useNavigate`\n\nIf you want to dive deeper into any of these files or want me to outline the exact changes needed for a specific file, let me know (and switch to Agent mode if you'd like me to implement them).",
