  "model": "claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a summary of the React Router v5 to v6 upgrade guide:\n\n## Upgrade Path\n\nThe recommended migration is incremental, in three phases:\n\n1. **Upgrade to React 16.8+** (needed for hooks)\n2. **Upgrade to React Router v5.1** (bridge release)\n3. **Upgrade to React Router v6**\n\nA **backwards compatibility package** lets you run v5 and v6 in parallel, migrating one component at a time.\n\n## Key Breaking Changes\n\n### Routing\n- **`<Switch>` becomes `<Routes>`** — with automatic best-match ranking instead of order-based matching\n- **`<Route>` uses `element` prop** instead of `component` or `render` props: `<Route path=\"/users\" element={<Users />} />`\n- **Routes and Links are relative** — no more manually building paths from `match.url` / `match.path`\n- **Simplified path patterns** — only `:id` params and trailing `*` wildcards; no more regex syntax\n- **`<Route exact>` and `<Route strict>` are removed** — use trailing `*` for deep matching\n\n### Navigation\n- **`useHistory` becomes `useNavigate`** — `navigate(\"/path\")` instead of `history.push(\"/path\")`\n- **`<Redirect>` becomes `<Navigate>`** — note that `<Navigate>` defaults to push (v5's `<Redirect>` defaulted to replace)\n- **`go` / `goBack` / `goForward`** become `navigate(-1)`, `navigate(1)`, etc.\n\n### Links\n- **`<Link to>` values** are now always relative to the route, not the current URL\n- **`<Link state>`** is a separate prop: `<Link to=\"/home\" state={state} />`\n- **`<Link component>` prop removed** — use `useHref` + `useLinkClickHandler` hooks instead\n- **`<NavLink exact>` renamed to `<NavLink end>`**\n- **`activeClassName` / `activeStyle` removed** — use function-style `className` and `style` props\n\n### Other\n- **`useRouteMatch` becomes `useMatch`** with a required pattern argument and renamed options (`strict` → `end`, `sensitive` → `caseSensitive`)\n- **`matchPath` argument order reversed** — pattern object first, then pathname\n- **`react-router-config`** is now built-in via `useRoutes`\n- **`StaticRouter`** moves to `react-router-dom/server`\n- **`<Prompt>`** was initially removed but `useBlocker` and `unstable_usePrompt` have since been added back\n\n## TL;DR Pattern\n\n```jsx\n// v5\nconst history = useHistory();\nhistory.push(\"/home\");\n\n// v6\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\nnavigate(\"/home\");\n```\n\n```jsx\n// v5\n<Switch>\n  <Route path=\"/users\" component={Users} />\n</Switch>\n\n// v6\n<Routes>\n  <Route path=\"/users\" element={<Users />} />\n</Routes>\n```\n\nThe core philosophy shift is from **render props and HOCs** to **hooks and elements**, aligning with modern React patterns.",
