  "text": "\nHere’s what matters for adding a last-viewed timestamp to the dashboard browser.\n\n---\n\n## Files to Consider\n\n### Frontend – Browse Dashboards\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/BrowseDashboardsPage.tsx` | Main page; wires in `RecentlyViewedDashboards` and `BrowseView` |\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/components/RecentlyViewedDashboards.tsx` | Recently viewed section; good place to show timestamps |\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/components/BrowseView.tsx` | Folder tree view |\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/components/DashboardsTree.tsx` | Tree table (Name, Tags columns) |\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/components/NameCell.tsx` | Renders dashboard name/link in tree |\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/api/recentlyViewed.ts` | Fetches recently viewed dashboards |\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/api/services.ts` | `listDashboards()` for folder view |\n| `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/components/SearchView.tsx` | Search results table |\n\n### Frontend – Impression / View Tracking\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `public/app/core/services/impression_srv.ts` | Records dashboard views (UIDs only, no timestamps) |\n| `public/app/features/dashboard/services/DashboardLoaderSrv.ts` | Calls `impressionSrv.addDashboardImpression()` when a dashboard loads |\n\n### Frontend – Search / Data Model\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `public/app/features/search/service/types.ts` | `DashboardQueryResult`, `DashboardViewItem` |\n| `public/app/features/search/types.ts` | `DashboardViewItem` with `sortMeta`, `sortMetaName` |\n| `public/app/features/search/service/utils.ts` | `queryResultToViewItem()` – maps search results to view items |\n| `public/app/features/search/service/unified.ts` | Unified search; `SearchHit.field` for extra fields |\n| `public/app/features/search/service/sql.ts` | SQL search fallback |\n\n### Backend\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `pkg/services/sqlstore/migrator/snapshot/00-schema.sql` | `user_dashboard_views` table (schema only) |\n| `pkg/storage/unified/search/builders/dashboard.go` | Search index fields (views, errors, etc.) |\n| `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go` | `recentlyViewedDashboards` feature flag |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Considerations\n\n### 1. Two Sources of “Last Viewed” Data\n\n- **`impression_srv`** – Client-side only, stores UIDs in localStorage (`dashboard_impressions-{orgId}`). No timestamps, only order.\n- **`user_dashboard_views`** – DB table with `user_id`, `dashboard_id`, `viewed` (datetime), `org_id`, `dashboard_uid`. There is no Go code in this repo that writes to it; it may be legacy or used elsewhere (e.g. Enterprise).\n\n### 2. Where to Show the Timestamp\n\n- **Recently viewed section** – Easiest: extend `impression_srv` to store timestamps and show them in `RecentlyViewedDashboards` / `DashListItem`.\n- **Folder tree (BrowseView)** – Needs backend support: search/list APIs must return per-user last-viewed time for each dashboard.\n- **Search results** – Same as folder tree: backend must expose last-viewed in the search response.\n\n### 3. Dual Search Backends\n\n- **UnifiedSearcher** – Uses `/apis/dashboard.grafana.app/v0alpha1/.../search`; `SearchHit.field` can carry extra fields.\n- **SQLSearcher** – Uses `/api/search`; `DashboardSearchHit` has `sortMeta`, `sortMetaName`.\n- Both feed into `DashboardQueryResult` and `queryResultToViewItem()`, which already supports `sortMeta` / `sortMetaName` for extra display values.\n\n### 4. Feature Flag\n\n- `recentlyViewedDashboards` (experimental) controls the recently viewed section.\n- It is checked in `BrowseDashboardsPage.tsx` around line 48.\n\n### 5. Data Flow for Browse View\n\n```\nlistDashboards() → getGrafanaSearcher().search() → DashboardQueryResult[]\n  → queryResultToViewItem() → DashboardViewItem\n  → DashboardsTree → NameCell / TagsCell\n```\n\n`DashboardViewItem` already has `sortMeta` and `sortMetaName` for extra display data (e.g. “Views”). A last-viewed timestamp could follow the same pattern.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Options\n\n### Option A: Recently Viewed Only (Client-Side)\n\n1. Change `impression_srv.ts` to store `{ uid, timestamp }[]` instead of `string[]`.\n2. Update `getRecentlyViewedDashboards()` in `recentlyViewed.ts` to return timestamps.\n3. Update `RecentlyViewedDashboards.tsx` and `DashListItem` to show “Last viewed: X ago”.\n\n**Pros:** No backend changes.  \n**Cons:** Only for recently viewed section; data is per-browser, not per-user.\n\n### Option B: Backend-Driven (Full Browse + Search)\n\n1. Implement backend writes to `user_dashboard_views` when a dashboard is viewed (e.g. in `GetDashboard` or equivalent).\n2. Add an API to read last-viewed times for the current user (or extend search).\n3. Extend search/list APIs to include `last_viewed` (or similar) in the response.\n4. Update `queryResultToViewItem()` and `DashboardViewItem` to carry and display it.\n5. Add a “Last viewed” column or inline text in `DashboardsTree` and `SearchView`.\n\n**Pros:** Per-user, consistent across devices.  \n**Cons:** Requires backend work and possibly migrations.\n\n### Option C: Hybrid\n\n- Use Option A for the recently viewed section.\n- Use Option B later for folder tree and search if needed.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Recently viewed section:** `RecentlyViewedDashboards.tsx`, `recentlyViewed.ts`, `impression_srv.ts`, `DashListItem`.\n- **Folder tree:** `DashboardsTree.tsx`, `NameCell.tsx`, `api/services.ts`, `queryResultToViewItem()`.\n- **Search:** `SearchView.tsx`, `unified.ts`, `sql.ts`.\n- **Backend:** `user_dashboard_views` exists but is not written to in this repo; `dashboard.go` shows how extra fields are added to search.\n- **Feature flag:** `recentlyViewedDashboards` controls the recently viewed section.\n\nThe main design choice is whether to stay client-side (Option A) or add backend support (Option B) for per-user, cross-device last-viewed timestamps.",
