  "text": "Here's what I've implemented in `BookmarksPage.tsx`:\n\n**Category Assignment** -- A `CATEGORY_SECTION_MAP` maps nav tree section IDs to three categories:\n  - **Content** -- dashboards, explore, starred, scenes, playlists, snapshots, library-panels\n  - **Operations** -- alerting, connections, monitoring, infrastructure, datasources\n  - **Admin** -- admin, cfg, users, teams, orgs, serviceaccounts, apikeys, plugins, server-settings, authentication, storage\n\nThe `findSectionForUrl` function walks the nav tree to determine which top-level section a bookmarked URL belongs to, and maps it to the appropriate category.\n\n**RadioButtonGroup Filter** -- A `RadioButtonGroup` at the top of the page lets users filter by \"All\", \"Content\", \"Operations\", or \"Admin\". Each option shows the count of bookmarks in that category (e.g., \"Content (3)\"). This follows the same pattern used in `UserListAdminPage` and `ConnectData`.\n\n**Grouped Rendering** -- When \"All\" is selected, bookmarks are grouped under section headers with a colored icon, label, and count pill. When a specific category is selected, only those bookmarks are shown without the header. Each card gets a color-coded border via the `NavLandingPageCard` `category` prop (`primary` for Content, `success` for Operations, `warning` for Admin), which leverages the existing category styling already built into that component.\n\n**Empty State** -- If no bookmarks match the active filter, a \"No bookmarks in this category\" empty state is shown.",
