  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the Grafana codebase and the React Router v5-to-v6 migration.\n\n---\n\n## Codebase Overview\n\nGrafana is a large **monorepo** with a **Go backend** and **TypeScript/React frontend**, organized into feature-based modules.\n\n### Top-Level Structure\n\n| Directory | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `pkg/` | Go backend — services, APIs, infrastructure (~75 service packages) |\n| `public/app/` | React/TypeScript frontend — ~53 feature modules |\n| `apps/` | Microservices (22 apps: dashboard, alerting, IAM, etc.) |\n| `packages/` | Shared npm packages (15 total: `grafana-ui`, `grafana-data`, `grafana-runtime`, etc.) |\n| `conf/` | Configuration files |\n| `devenv/` | Development environment (Docker, etc.) |\n| `e2e/` / `e2e-playwright/` | End-to-end tests |\n| `scripts/` / `tools/` | Build and development utilities |\n\n### Frontend (`public/app/`)\n\nThe frontend is organized by feature area:\n\n- **`features/`** — The bulk of the UI: `dashboard`, `dashboard-scene`, `alerting`, `explore`, `datasources`, `browse-dashboards`, `playlist`, `provisioning`, `bookmarks`, `plugins`, `scopes`, `variables`, etc.\n- **`core/`** — Core infrastructure: navigation, services (`keybindingSrv`), `AppChrome`, link click interception\n- **`routes/`** — Route definitions (`routes.tsx`) and the router wrapper (`RoutesWrapper.tsx`)\n- **`plugins/`** — Plugin system and built-in panel plugins\n- **`store/`** — Redux state management\n\n### Backend (`pkg/`)\n\n- **`services/`** — Business logic (~75 services: `dashboards`, `alerting`, `auth`, `featuremgmt`, etc.)\n- **`api/`** — HTTP API handlers\n- **`apiserver/`** — Kubernetes-style API server\n- **`registry/`** — Resource registry for K8s-style APIs\n- **`middleware/`** — HTTP middleware (auth, logging, etc.)\n\n### Build System\n\nKey commands via `Makefile`: `make build`, `make build-go`, `make build-js`, `make gen-go` (wire DI), `make gen-feature-toggles`, `make test`.\n\n---\n\n## React Router Migration: v5 to v6\n\n### Current Architecture — Transitional Hybrid\n\nGrafana runs a **v5 Router at the root** with a **v5-compat bridge** that enables v6 APIs inside the v5 tree:\n\n```\n<Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>     ← React Router v5\n  <LocationServiceProvider>\n    <CompatRouter>                                   ← v5-compat bridge\n      <Routes> / <Route>                             ← v6 API via compat\n        <GrafanaRouteWrapper>                        ← auth + rendering\n          <Page Component>\n```\n\nBoth navigation patterns work because they share the same `history` instance owned by `locationService`.\n\n| Layer | Package | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| Outer router | `react-router-dom` v5.3.4 | Root `<Router>` with `history` v4 |\n| Compat bridge | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` v6.26.1 | Enables v6 hooks inside v5 tree |\n| Legacy navigation | `locationService` singleton | `push()`, `replace()`, `partial()` |\n| Modern navigation | `useNavigate()` hook | From v5-compat — the target API |\n\n### Migration Status (Live Snapshot)\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|---|---|\n| **Not migrated** (legacy `locationService` only) | **122 files** |\n| **Partially migrated** (both patterns) | **1 file** |\n| **Fully migrated** (`useNavigate` only) | **16 files** |\n| **Feature flags registered** | **0** |\n\nThat's roughly **~10% migrated** by file count.\n\n### Breakdown by Feature Area\n\n| Area | Legacy Files | Migrated Files | Status |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| **Dashboard (legacy + scene)** | 53 | 0 | Not started |\n| **Alerting** | 20 | 1 | Early |\n| **Provisioning** | 1 | 14 | Nearly complete |\n| **Core infrastructure** | 8 | 0 | Not started |\n| **Playlist** | 4 | 0 | Not started |\n| **Variables** | 4 | 0 | Not started |\n| **Explore** | 4 | 0 | Not started |\n| **Scopes** | 3 | 0 | Not started |\n| **Browse Dashboards** | 3 | 0 | Not started |\n| **Other** | 22 | 1 | Early |\n\n### What's Been Migrated\n\nThe **provisioning** feature is the furthest along (14 of 15 files). This includes `ConfigForm`, `ConnectionForm`, `ProvisioningWizard`, delete/move/save forms, and wizard navigation hooks. A handful of other files have been migrated individually (`UserCreatePage`, an alerting modal, and a GOps component).\n\n### Migration Pattern\n\nEach migration is intended to be **gated behind a feature flag** for safe rollout, following the naming convention `{feature}UseNavigate`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { config, locationService } from '@grafana/runtime';\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\n\nif (config.featureToggles.playlistUseNavigate) {\n  navigate('/playlists');\n} else {\n  locationService.push('/playlists');\n}\n```\n\nFeature flags are defined in `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go` and auto-generated to TypeScript via `make gen-feature-toggles`. Notably, no `UseNavigate` feature flags have been registered yet — the provisioning area migrated directly without them.\n\n### Key Risks and Challenges\n\n1. **Dashboard surface area is massive.** 53 files across `features/dashboard/` and `features/dashboard-scene/` are tightly coupled to Scenes and legacy state management, making this the most complex migration target.\n\n2. **Non-React code can't use hooks.** Files like `keybindingSrv.ts`, `interceptLinkClicks.ts`, `PlaylistSrv.ts`, and various Redux action files aren't React components. They need an architectural change (e.g., passing `navigate` as a parameter or using a context/provider pattern).\n\n3. **`locationService.partial()` has no v6 equivalent.** 54 files use `partial()` for query-param-only updates. A utility wrapper on top of `useNavigate` + `useLocation` will need to be built.\n\n4. **The global link click interceptor** (`interceptLinkClicks.ts`) funnels all `<a>` clicks through `locationService.push()`. This must be replaced with a React Router-aware mechanism before `locationService` can be fully removed.\n\n5. **Test files assert against `locationService.getLocation()`.** Each migration requires updating tests to mock `useNavigate` instead.\n\n### Target End State\n\n```\n<BrowserRouter>                    ← React Router v6 (native)\n  <Routes>\n    <Route element={...} />\n  </Routes>\n  Navigation: useNavigate() only\n  Location:   useLocation() only\n  Params:     useParams() only\n```\n\nThe migration removes the v5 Router, the CompatRouter bridge, the `locationService` singleton as a navigation mechanism, and the global link click interceptor.\n\n### Key Files\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Root router setup (v5 + compat bridge) |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Route definitions |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | `locationService` singleton |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` | Global link click interception |\n| `public/app/core/services/keybindingSrv.ts` | Keyboard shortcuts (non-React) |\n| `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go` | Feature flag definitions |\n| `.cursor/skills/react-router-migration/SKILL.md` | Step-by-step contributor guide |\n\n### Recommended Next Migration Targets\n\nThe easiest wins are small, isolated form pages with simple post-submit redirects:\n\n1. `features/playlist/PlaylistEditPage.tsx` — single redirect after save\n2. `features/playlist/PlaylistNewPage.tsx` — same pattern\n3. `features/teams/CreateTeam.tsx` — form with redirect on success\n4. `features/serviceaccounts/ServiceAccountCreatePage.tsx` — isolated form page\n5. `features/org/UserInviteForm.tsx` — single post-submit redirect",
