  "text": "Both pages are very straightforward -- each has a single `locationService.push('/playlists')` call after a form submission. Here's a simple Mermaid diagram:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"Current State (locationService)\"\n        A1[PlaylistNewPage] -->|user submits form| B1[createPlaylist mutation]\n        B1 --> C1[\"locationService.push('/playlists')\"]\n        C1 --> D1[/playlists list page/]\n\n        A2[PlaylistEditPage] -->|user submits form| B2[replacePlaylist mutation]\n        B2 --> C2[\"locationService.push('/playlists')\"]\n        C2 --> D1\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Target State (useNavigate)\"\n        A3[PlaylistNewPage] -->|user submits form| B3[createPlaylist mutation]\n        B3 --> C3[\"navigate('/playlists')\"]\n        C3 --> D2[/playlists list page/]\n\n        A4[PlaylistEditPage] -->|user submits form| B4[replacePlaylist mutation]\n        B4 --> C4[\"navigate('/playlists')\"]\n        C4 --> D2\n    end\n\n    style C1 fill:#f66,color:#fff\n    style C2 fill:#f66,color:#fff\n    style C3 fill:#4a4,color:#fff\n    style C4 fill:#4a4,color:#fff\n```\n\nBoth pages share the exact same pattern: a form component (`PlaylistForm`) calls `onSubmit`, which fires an API mutation and then redirects to `/playlists`. The migration is a one-for-one swap of `locationService.push` (red) with `navigate` from the `useNavigate` hook (green), gated behind a feature flag during the transition.",
