  "text": "\nHere are the main files involved in the Bookmarks page UI:\n\n---\n\n## Core page component\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/app/features/bookmarks/BookmarksPage.tsx`** | Main page component: layout, empty state, grid of bookmark cards, and grid styles (`gridTemplateColumns`, `gridAutoRows`, spacing). |\n\n---\n\n## Card component\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/app/core/components/NavLandingPage/NavLandingPageCard.tsx`** | Card used for each bookmark: heading, description, link, optional `category` styling (primary/secondary/success/warning/error), and card layout. |\n\n---\n\n## Data and utilities\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/hooks.ts`** | `usePinnedItems()` – returns pinned/bookmarked URLs from user preferences. |\n| **`public/app/core/components/AppChrome/MegaMenu/utils.ts`** | `findByUrl()` – finds nav items by URL in the nav tree. |\n\n---\n\n## Shared layout and UI\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/app/core/components/Page/Page.tsx`** | Page wrapper and chrome integration. |\n| **`packages/grafana-ui/src/components/EmptyState/EmptyState.tsx`** | Empty state when there are no bookmarks. |\n\n---\n\n## Routing and navigation\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/app/routes/routes.tsx`** (lines 537–541) | Route definition for `/bookmarks`. |\n| **`public/app/core/reducers/navBarTree.ts`** | Nav tree used to resolve bookmark URLs to nav items. |\n\n---\n\n## Localization\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **`public/locales/en-US/grafana.json`** | Strings for `bookmarks-page.empty.message` and `bookmarks-page.empty.tip`. |\n\n---\n\n## Suggested starting points\n\n- **Layout and structure:** `BookmarksPage.tsx`\n- **Card appearance:** `NavLandingPageCard.tsx`\n- **Empty state:** `BookmarksPage.tsx` (EmptyState usage) and `EmptyState.tsx`\n- **Data source:** `hooks.ts` (`usePinnedItems`) and `utils.ts` (`findByUrl`)\n\n`NavLandingPageCard` is shared with `NavLandingPage.tsx` (used for other nav landing pages). Changes there will affect both.",
