  "model": "composer-1.5",
  "text": "\nHere are the main implications of making more substantial changes to the bookmarks page beyond cosmetic updates:\n\n---\n\n## 1. **Data model & storage**\n\nBookmarks are stored as **URL strings** in user preferences under `navbar.bookmarkUrls`.\n\n| Layer | File(s) | Implication |\n|-------|---------|-------------|\n| **Backend model** | `pkg/services/preference/model.go` | `NavbarPreference` has `BookmarkUrls []string`. Changing to richer data (e.g. labels, order, custom names) means updating this struct and any DB migration. |\n| **Generated schema** | `packages/grafana-schema/src/raw/preferences/x/preferences_types.gen.ts` | Types are generated from CUE; edit the source schema and run `make gen-cue`. |\n| **API types** | `packages/grafana-api-clients/.../endpoints.gen.ts` | `PatchPrefsCmd` and related types are generated from OpenAPI; they follow the backend schema. |\n| **K8s-style API** | `apps/preferences/pkg/apis/preferences/v1alpha1/` | New preferences API; schema changes here affect both legacy and new APIs. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. **MegaMenu (pin/unpin)**\n\nThe MegaMenu is the main place where bookmarks are created and removed.\n\n| File | Role | Implication |\n|------|------|-------------|\n| **`MegaMenu.tsx`** | Uses `usePinnedItems`, `onPinItem`, `patchPreferences` | Any change to bookmark shape (e.g. `{ url, label }`) requires updating how `onPinItem` builds `newItems` and what it sends to `patchPreferences`. |\n| **`MegaMenuItem.tsx`** | Renders pin button and calls `onPin(link)` | Only needs changes if you add bookmark-specific UI (e.g. edit label) in the menu. |\n| **`hooks.ts`** | `usePinnedItems()` returns `bookmarkUrls` | If the model changes, this hook must return the new structure. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. **Redux state**\n\n| File | Role | Implication |\n|------|------|-------------|\n| **`navBarTree.ts`** | `setBookmark` reducer | Keeps the nav tree’s “bookmarks” section in sync after pin/unpin. It expects `NavModelItem` and `url`. Changing the bookmark model may require updating this reducer. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. **Shared components**\n\n| Component | Used by | Implication |\n|-----------|---------|-------------|\n| **`NavLandingPageCard`** | `BookmarksPage`, `NavLandingPage` (drilldown, apps, cfg, etc.) | Changes to card layout or props affect all nav landing pages. Consider a `BookmarkCard` wrapper if you need bookmark-specific behavior. |\n| **`NavLandingPage`** | Many nav sections (drilldown, apps, cfg, infrastructure, etc.) | Only relevant if you change shared patterns used by both bookmarks and other landing pages. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. **Nav tree dependency**\n\nBookmarks are resolved via `findByUrl(navTree, url)`:\n\n- Bookmarks are only valid if their URL exists in the nav tree.\n- If a nav item is removed or its URL changes, the bookmark becomes invalid and is dropped.\n- `findByUrl` is used by both `BookmarksPage` and `MegaMenu`.\n\nIf you add custom labels or metadata, you may need to handle cases where `findByUrl` returns `null` (e.g. show a fallback card or a “broken” bookmark state).\n\n---\n\n## 6. **Example change types and impact**\n\n| Change | Likely impact |\n|--------|----------------|\n| **Custom labels** | Backend model, schema, API, `usePinnedItems`, MegaMenu `onPinItem`, BookmarksPage display. |\n| **Reordering** | Backend model (e.g. ordered array or explicit `order`), MegaMenu `onPinItem`, BookmarksPage sort order. |\n| **Categories/tags** | Backend model, schema, `usePinnedItems`, BookmarksPage grouping/filtering. |\n| **Unpin from Bookmarks page** | Add unpin action in `BookmarksPage`, reuse `patchPreferences` (or equivalent) and `setBookmark` logic from MegaMenu. |\n| **Bookmarks for non-nav URLs** | `findByUrl` will fail; need a different resolution path or a separate “custom bookmark” type. |\n\n---\n\n## 7. **Testing**\n\n| Area | Files |\n|------|-------|\n| **Backend** | `pkg/api/preferences_test.go` – add/update tests for new preference shapes. |\n| **MegaMenu utils** | `MegaMenu/utils.test.ts` – `findByUrl` and related helpers. |\n| **NavLandingPage** | `NavLandingPage.test.tsx`, `NavLandingPageCard.test.tsx` – if you change shared components. |\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Cosmetic / layout changes** → Mostly `BookmarksPage.tsx` and possibly `NavLandingPageCard.tsx`.\n- **Data model changes** → Backend (`model.go`), generated schema, API clients, `hooks.ts`, MegaMenu, and `navBarTree` reducer.\n- **New features (unpin, reorder, labels)** → Same as data model, plus UI in `BookmarksPage` and/or MegaMenu.\n\nThe main coupling is that bookmarks are stored as a simple list of URLs in user preferences and resolved against the nav tree. Any richer model will propagate through preferences, API, MegaMenu, and BookmarksPage.",
