  "model": "composer-1.5",
  "text": "\nHere’s an overview of the codebase and React Router architecture, plus concrete migration targets.\n\n---\n\n# Grafana Codebase Overview\n\n## High-level structure\n\nGrafana is a React/TypeScript frontend with a Go backend. The frontend lives mainly under `public/app/`:\n\n- **`public/app/core/`** – shared services, navigation, AppChrome, providers\n- **`public/app/features/`** – feature modules (dashboards, alerting, provisioning, playlists, etc.)\n- **`public/app/routes/`** – route definitions and router setup\n- **`packages/grafana-runtime/`** – runtime services, including `locationService`\n\n---\n\n# React Router Architecture\n\n## Current hybrid setup\n\nGrafana uses a **v5/v6 hybrid**:\n\n```\nAppWrapper\n  └── RouterWrapper (RoutesWrapper.tsx)\n        └── <Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>   ← React Router v5\n              └── LocationServiceProvider\n                    └── <CompatRouter>                        ← react-router-dom-v5-compat\n                          └── <Routes> / <Route>             ← v6 API\n                                └── GrafanaRouteWrapper → Page components\n```\n\nImportant pieces:\n\n| Layer | Package | Role |\n|-------|---------|------|\n| Root router | `react-router-dom` v5.3.4 | `<Router history={...}>` |\n| History | `history` v4 via `locationService` | Single shared history instance |\n| Compat bridge | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` v6.26.1 | `<CompatRouter>` enables v6 hooks inside v5 tree |\n| Routes | v6 `<Routes>` / `<Route>` | Route matching and rendering |\n| Legacy nav | `locationService` singleton | `push()`, `replace()`, `partial()` |\n| Modern nav | `useNavigate()` from v5-compat | Declarative navigation |\n\nBoth `locationService` and `useNavigate` use the same history instance, so they can coexist.\n\n## Main files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Root router (v5 `Router` + `CompatRouter`) |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | Route definitions via `getAppRoutes()` |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` | Global `<a>` clicks → `locationService.push()` |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | `locationService` singleton |\n\n## Migration status (approx.)\n\n- **~145 files** – only `locationService` (legacy)\n- **~16 files** – only `useNavigate` (migrated)\n- **~1 file** – both (partially migrated)\n\nProvisioning is mostly migrated; dashboards, alerting, and playlists are not.\n\n---\n\n# Suggested small-scale migration targets\n\nThese are good candidates for a first migration pass because they:\n\n- Use React components (hooks can be used)\n- Have a single `locationService.push()` or `replace()`\n- Are small and isolated\n\n## 1. `PlaylistEditPage.tsx` (simplest)\n\n**Path:** `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistEditPage.tsx`\n\n- Single `locationService.push('/playlists')` after form submit (around line 26)\n- Same pattern as `UserCreatePage.tsx`, which is already migrated\n\n**Change:** Add `useNavigate`, replace `locationService.push` with `navigate('/playlists')` (optionally behind a feature flag).\n\n---\n\n## 2. `PlaylistNewPage.tsx`\n\n**Path:** `public/app/features/playlist/PlaylistNewPage.tsx`\n\n- Same pattern as `PlaylistEditPage`: one `locationService.push('/playlists')` after create (around line 21)\n- Very small file (~40 lines)\n\n---\n\n## 3. `ServiceAccountCreatePage.tsx`\n\n**Path:** `public/app/features/serviceaccounts/ServiceAccountCreatePage.tsx`\n\n- Single `locationService.push(\\`/org/serviceaccounts/${response.uid}\\`)` after create (around line 105)\n- Similar to `UserCreatePage.tsx` (already migrated)\n- Slightly more complex due to form handling and role picker\n\n---\n\n## 4. `CreateNewButton.tsx` (browse-dashboards)\n\n**Path:** `public/app/features/browse-dashboards/components/CreateNewButton.tsx`\n\n- Single `locationService.push(...)` in `onCreateFolder` (around line 89)\n- Uses `locationUtil.stripBaseFromUrl(folder.data.url)` for the target URL\n- Good example of navigation after an async operation (folder creation)\n\n---\n\n## 5. `StartModal.tsx` (playlist)\n\n**Path:** `public/app/features/playlist/StartModal.tsx`\n\n- Single `locationService.push(urlUtil.renderUrl(...))` to start a playlist\n- Slightly more involved because of URL building with params\n\n---\n\n# Migration pattern (from the skill)\n\n```typescript\n// Before\nimport { locationService } from '@grafana/runtime';\nlocationService.push('/path');\n\n// After (with feature flag)\nimport { config, locationService } from '@grafana/runtime';\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\n\nif (config.featureToggles.playlistUseNavigate) {\n  navigate('/path');\n} else {\n  locationService.push('/path');\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n# Files to avoid for now\n\n- **`BookmarksPage.tsx`** – Uses `NavLandingPageCard` with `href`; navigation is via links, not `locationService`\n- **`PlaylistCard.tsx`** – Uses `LinkButton` with `href`; no `locationService` usage\n- **`keybindingSrv.ts`**, **`interceptLinkClicks.ts`** – Non-React services; need a different approach (e.g. context or refactoring)\n- **`locationService.partial()`** – No direct `useNavigate` equivalent; needs a custom helper\n\n---\n\n# Suggested order for testing\n\n1. **`PlaylistEditPage.tsx`** – Smallest, clearest case\n2. **`PlaylistNewPage.tsx`** – Same pattern, quick second step\n3. **`CreateNewButton.tsx`** – Different context (browse-dashboards) and async flow\n\nFor each, add a feature flag in `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go`, run `make gen-feature-toggles`, then apply the dual-path pattern above. The migration skill at `.cursor/skills/react-router-migration/SKILL.md` has the full workflow and testing patterns.",
