  "model": "claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a comprehensive overview of the Grafana codebase and its React Router migration.\n\n---\n\n## Codebase Overview\n\nGrafana is a large monorepo. The frontend lives in `public/app/`, with feature areas organized under `public/app/features/` (dashboards, alerting, explore, provisioning, playlist, etc.). The backend is Go under `pkg/`. Routing is entirely frontend-side (SPA).\n\n---\n\n## Current Routing Architecture — The Hybrid Bridge\n\nThe app uses a **transitional hybrid architecture** that layers React Router v5, a shared `history` instance, and a v6 compat layer. The entry point is `RoutesWrapper.tsx`:\n\n```1:56:public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx\nimport { ComponentType, ReactNode, type JSX } from 'react';\nimport { Router } from 'react-router-dom';\nimport { CompatRouter } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n\nimport { locationService, LocationServiceProvider } from '@grafana/runtime';\n// ...\n\nexport function RouterWrapper(props: RouterWrapperProps) {\n  return (\n    <Router history={locationService.getHistory()}>\n      <LocationServiceProvider service={locationService}>\n        <CompatRouter>\n          ...\n          {props.routes}\n          ...\n        </CompatRouter>\n      </LocationServiceProvider>\n    </Router>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe three layers from outermost to innermost:\n\n| Layer | Package | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `<Router history={...}>` | `react-router-dom` v5.3.4 | Root router consuming `history` v4 |\n| `locationService` | `@grafana/runtime` singleton | Owns the `history` instance; imperative `push/replace/partial` API |\n| `<CompatRouter>` | `react-router-dom-v5-compat` v6.26.1 | Enables v6 hooks (`useNavigate`, `useLocation`, `useParams`) inside the v5 tree |\n\nBoth old and new navigation APIs work because they share the **same underlying `history` object** owned by `locationService`. This is the key insight of the bridge.\n\nBelow `CompatRouter`, routes are defined with v6 `<Routes>`/`<Route>` in `public/app/routes/routes.tsx`, each wrapped by `GrafanaRoute` (which handles auth, access control, error boundaries, and analytics).\n\n---\n\n## The Two Navigation Patterns\n\n**Legacy (still used in ~89% of navigation files):**\n```typescript\nimport { locationService } from '@grafana/runtime';\n\nlocationService.push('/d/abc123');\nlocationService.replace('/search');\nlocationService.partial({ refresh: '5s' }); // query-param-only update\n```\n\n**Modern (used in migrated files):**\n```typescript\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\nnavigate('/d/abc123');\nnavigate(-1); // go back\n```\n\n---\n\n## Migration Progress\n\n```\nLegacy only (locationService)  ████████████████████  145 files (89%)\nMigrated (useNavigate)         ██                     16 files (10%)\nPartially migrated             ▏                       1 file  (<1%)\n```\n\n**By feature area:**\n\n| Area | Legacy files | Migrated | Status |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| Dashboards (dashboard + dashboard-scene + browse-dashboards) | 67 | 0 | Not started |\n| Alerting | 22 | 1 | Early |\n| Provisioning | 2 | 14 | Nearly complete |\n| Scopes | 6 | 0 | Not started |\n| Playlist | 5 | 0 | Not started |\n| Variables | 5 | 0 | Not started |\n| Explore | 4 | 0 | Not started |\n| Core (keybindings, chrome, navigation) | 8 | 0 | Not started |\n\n**Provisioning** is the furthest along — it migrated directly to `useNavigate` without feature flags. You can see the pattern clearly in `useWizardNavigation.ts`:\n\n```2:45:public/app/features/provisioning/Wizard/hooks/useWizardNavigation.ts\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n// ...\nexport function useWizardNavigation(...): UseWizardNavigationReturn {\n  const navigate = useNavigate();\n  // ...\n  navigate(PROVISIONING_URL); // called on wizard completion\n```\n\n---\n\n## Migration Strategy\n\n### Feature flag pattern (for larger surfaces)\nFuture migrations of high-traffic areas like dashboards will use a `{feature}UseNavigate` flag to allow safe, incremental rollout:\n\n```typescript\nimport { config, locationService } from '@grafana/runtime';\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom-v5-compat';\n\nconst navigate = useNavigate();\n\nif (config.featureToggles.dashboardUseNavigate) {\n  navigate('/d/abc123');\n} else {\n  locationService.push('/d/abc123');\n}\n```\n\nOne flag already exists in the feature toggle registry: `playlistUseNavigate` (in `packages/grafana-data/src/types/featureToggles.gen.ts`), making the playlist area the next likely migration candidate.\n\n---\n\n## Key Technical Challenges\n\n1. **`locationService.partial()` has no direct equivalent.** 54 files use it for query-param-only updates. There's no built-in `useNavigate` equivalent — a utility wrapper will need to be built combining `useNavigate` + `useLocation`.\n\n2. **Non-React code can't use hooks.** Files like `keybindingSrv.ts`, `interceptLinkClicks.ts`, and `AppChromeService.tsx` are services/utilities, not React components. They'll need architectural rethinking (e.g., receiving a `navigate` function via dependency injection).\n\n3. **The global link click interceptor.** `public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` intercepts all `<a>` clicks app-wide and routes them through `locationService.push()`. This must be replaced before the old router can be removed.\n\n4. **Test surface.** Many tests assert against `locationService.getLocation()`. Each migrated component requires updating its test to mock `useNavigate` instead.\n\n---\n\n## Target End State\n\nOnce the migration is complete, the entire hybrid bridge collapses into native React Router v6:\n\n```\n<BrowserRouter>          ← replaces <Router history={...}> + <CompatRouter>\n  <Routes>\n    <Route ... />\n  </Routes>\n</BrowserRouter>\n\nNavigation: useNavigate() only\nLocation:   useLocation() only\nParams:     useParams() only\n```\n\nThe `locationService` singleton, the v5 `<Router>`, the `<CompatRouter>`, and `interceptLinkClicks.ts` are all deleted.\n\n---\n\n## Key Files to Know\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `public/app/routes/RoutesWrapper.tsx` | Root router setup — the hybrid bridge |\n| `public/app/routes/routes.tsx` | All route definitions (`getAppRoutes()`) |\n| `public/app/AppWrapper.tsx` | App root, provider hierarchy |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/GrafanaRoute.tsx` | Route wrapper (auth, analytics, error boundary) |\n| `public/app/core/navigation/patch/interceptLinkClicks.ts` | Global `<a>` → `locationService.push()` interceptor |\n| `packages/grafana-runtime/src/services/LocationService.tsx` | The `locationService` singleton |\n| `pkg/services/featuremgmt/registry.go` | Feature flag definitions |\n| `docs/react-router-migration-overview.md` | Migration tracking doc |",
