  "model": "claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking",
  "text": "Here's a Mermaid diagram showing the relationship between `locationService` and React Router using a handful of concrete files:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph history[\"Shared history instance (history v4)\"]\n        H[/\"history object\"/]\n    end\n\n    subgraph runtime[\"@grafana/runtime\"]\n        LS[\"locationService\\n(LocationService.tsx)\\n\\n.push() .replace() .partial()\\n.getHistory()\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph RoutesWrapper[\"RoutesWrapper.tsx  —  the hybrid bridge\"]\n        RV5[\"&lt;Router history={locationService.getHistory()}&gt;\\nreact-router-dom v5\"]\n        LSP[\"&lt;LocationServiceProvider&gt;\"]\n        CR[\"&lt;CompatRouter&gt;\\nreact-router-dom-v5-compat\"]\n        RV6[\"&lt;Routes&gt; / &lt;Route&gt;\\n(v6 API)\"]\n        RV5 --> LSP --> CR --> RV6\n    end\n\n    subgraph legacy[\"Legacy pattern  (still ~89% of files)\"]\n        ILC[\"interceptLinkClicks.ts\\n\\nAll &lt;a&gt; clicks → locationService.push()\"]\n        UUP[\"hooks.ts · useUrlParams()\\n\\nuseLocation() for reads\\nlocationService.partial() for writes\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph modern[\"Modern pattern  (migrated files)\"]\n        WN[\"useWizardNavigation.ts\\n(provisioning)\\n\\nconst navigate = useNavigate()\\nnavigate(PROVISIONING_URL)\"]\n    end\n\n    %% locationService owns the history object\n    LS -- \".getHistory()\" --> H\n\n    %% v5 Router consumes it\n    H -- \"consumed by\" --> RV5\n\n    %% CompatRouter makes v6 hooks available\n    CR -- \"enables useNavigate()\\nuseLocation()\\nuseParams()\" --> modern\n\n    %% legacy consumers call locationService directly\n    ILC -- \"locationService.push()\" --> LS\n    UUP -- \"locationService.partial()\" --> LS\n\n    %% useUrlParams reads from React Router\n    CR -- \"useLocation()\" --> UUP\n\n    %% Both paths mutate the same history\n    LS -- \"mutates\" --> H\n    modern -- \"mutates via\\ncompat hook\" --> H\n```\n\n### Reading the diagram\n\n- **The `history` object** (centre-top) is the single source of truth that both patterns share. That's why they can coexist without conflicts.\n- **`locationService`** wraps `history` and exposes the imperative API (`push`, `replace`, `partial`). It also hands the `history` object to the v5 `<Router>`.\n- **`RoutesWrapper.tsx`** is the bridge: the outer v5 `<Router>` consumes the same `history`, then `<CompatRouter>` inside it unlocks all the v6 hooks.\n- **`interceptLinkClicks.ts`** — every bare `<a>` click in the app goes through this global handler and calls `locationService.push()`. It never touches React Router at all.\n- **`hooks.ts · useUrlParams`** is a telling half-and-half example: it reads location state via the v6 `useLocation()` hook, but writes via `locationService.partial()` — the comment in the source even says *\"Should find a way to use history directly here\"*.\n- **`useWizardNavigation.ts`** (provisioning) shows the fully migrated pattern — `useNavigate()` only, no `locationService` in sight.",
